@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch11ch12-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch11ch12-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 11 and 12"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch11ch12-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch11ch12_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.0.0 (2026-11-10): Mission stage. Opened as its own narrow lineage rather than widening Lineage3's mission: per the owner's standing rule to prefer simple, narrow, closeable lineages over one broad package-wide lineage, and per Lineage3's own Scope3 exclusion (ex:Excl3_OtherChapters, 2026-11-08) stating chapters 11 onward get their own narrow lineages. Routed per G195: this is not a gap in Lineage3's mission (chapters 9-10 only), so it is not a change request there; it is new, non-urgent work, so it opens as its own lineage rather than waiting - the work is agent-paced, not calendar-paced, so nothing requires Lineage3's one remaining item (TK_Ret_Ch09_Research/_Verify) to close first." .

## --- Profile declaration (ceremony step 1) ---

ex:ProfileDecl4 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3 (ex:ProfileDecl, 2026-11-08): work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work and this lineage names none other. Level L2 stated plainly because this lineage does not re-run the full SHACL/register tooling used by the BRSF framework's own self-governance against this course repository's simplified lineage files." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-10T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date .

## --- Lineage ---

ex:Lineage4 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 11 and 12, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission4 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 4 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl4 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 is the closed SEN0414 slides lineage. Unlike chapters 9-10, chapters 11 and 12 had no Ready items naming them at Lineage2's closure (CLOSURE_REPORT_sen0414_slides_lineage_Lineage2_v1_0_0.md section 2 names only the chapter-9/10 items as carried forward): TK_Ret_Ch11_Research/_Verify/_Page_Build/_Page_Verify/_Deck_Build/_Deck_Verify and the chapter-12 equivalents were all recorded Done by 2026-10-26 (sen0414_slides_lineage_v2_402_0.ttl, comments 2.240.0-2.274.0), before Lineage2 closed. This lineage therefore carries forward no open item; it opens fresh on a mission the owner is stating now, parallel to, not continuing, Lineage3."@en .

## --- Mission ---

ex:Mission4 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 11 and 12 taught from one approved draft each"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog4 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Chapters 11 (Organizing Files) and 12 (Designing and Deploying Command Line Programs) of the third edition are taught with a deck and an interactive page, each produced from one owner-approved chapter draft, following the same review the owner asked for and received on chapters 9 and 10 this week: a true, sourced, pedagogically-motivated story (per the owner's 2026-11-09 principle - story count is not preset, but important history of the concepts must be covered within time and scope), an accurate resources slide, and any open items named and closed before build." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction this conversation, 2026-11-10 ('Now, let's plan next 2 chapters'), following the Lineage3 pattern and its own stated exclusion that later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages, rather than widening Lineage3's mission." .
